WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.493
A batch job posts three payments to the ledger.

2
00:00:05.493 --> 00:00:09.177
Each emit sits in a try/catch that logs the error and goes on.

3
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.038
The ledger refuses pay-2, which has a negative amount.

4
00:00:13.038 --> 00:00:14.789
Which payments get posted?

5
00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:18.702
pay-1 is posted.

6
00:00:18.702 --> 00:00:23.953
pay-2 makes the ledger throw, back up through emit, and the catch logs it.

7
00:00:23.953 --> 00:00:24.733
As planned.

8
00:00:24.933 --> 00:00:27.382
But pay-3 never reaches the ledger.

9
00:00:27.382 --> 00:00:32.349
emit refuses it, the catch logs that too, and collect returns normally.

10
00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:38.483
flow { } puts a SafeCollector between your block and your collector: an inspector at the serving hatch.

11
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.175
It checks every plate.

12
00:00:40.175 --> 00:00:41.919
Is the kitchen still open?

13
00:00:41.919 --> 00:00:45.340
Is it the same kitchen, with the same cook's badge?

14
00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:46.949
Did the last emit throw?

15
00:00:46.949 --> 00:00:49.229
Any wrong answer, and emit throws.

16
00:00:49.433 --> 00:00:51.110
Check three refused pay-3.

17
00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:56.593
The inspector never looks at the food, only at who emits and how the last plate went.

18
00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:02.546
The library's own map, filter, take, flowOf and asFlow skip the inspector.

19
00:01:02.546 --> 00:01:08.479
They are built with unsafeFlow: trusted staff, one plain call per value, and no checks.

20
00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.720
How does take(2) stop the cook?

21
00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.066
It has no handle on the cook's loop.

22
00:01:13.066 --> 00:01:14.565
All it can do is throw.

23
00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:20.702
After the second plate, take throws a red card, an AbortFlowException with its own name on it.

24
00:01:20.702 --> 00:01:24.807
It flies back up through every emit, and the cook's finally runs.

25
00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:28.751
take catches it, checks the name, and ends the flow quietly.

26
00:01:28.751 --> 00:01:31.105
A card with another name would fly on.

27
00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:35.658
The try/catch around emit catches the red card too.

28
00:01:35.658 --> 00:01:40.288
The cook emits again, the inspector refuses, and the catch logs it.

29
00:01:40.288 --> 00:01:43.951
With take(1) over 1,000 items, that's 1,000 warnings.

30
00:01:44.867 --> 00:01:46.194
This is Kotlin only.

31
00:01:46.194 --> 00:01:47.854
Keep emit out of any try.

32
00:01:47.854 --> 00:01:51.969
Catch the narrow error where it happens, inside the collector.

33
00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.831
So flow { } checks every emit.

34
00:01:54.831 --> 00:01:56.931
Never wrap emit in a try/catch.

35
00:01:57.133 --> 00:01:57.935
Quick check.

36
00:01:57.935 --> 00:02:02.681
A producer catches Throwable around emit, and the flow ends in take(1).

37
00:02:02.681 --> 00:02:04.620
What does its second emit do?
